 out exactly when to launch  this spin-off fantasy series and he  admits that the network was cautious  about revealing a date because of  everything happening with all of the  lockdowns the new series which comes  from george rr martin ryan condole and  miguel sapochnick has now finished  production and fans should expect an  update soon  now casey went on to say one of the  reasons why we're trying to be cautious  about it is when you're shooting a show  that big during a pandemic especially  with the last round with a lot of the  crew and cast members you don't know who  is going to drop out or if we're going  to have to shut down so we didn't want  to declare a date then find ourselves  shut down he said now that we are out of  production i think that we will discuss  this with our guys and figure out what  we want to do in regards of announcing a  date but i was just trying to make sure  that we didn't come out with a date that  we couldn't meet for something that was  out of our control casey also spoke  about the other successor shows that are  in various stages of development  deadline revealed last march that the  network was developing three different  ideas for new shows set within george rr  martin's fantasy world including 9  voyages aka the sea snake flea bottom  and 10 000 ships  steve conrad is also attached to write a  duncan egg series  casey blois said that there was nothing  to really report there but admitted that  some of them are beginning to look  really good it's just like any  development process  some are looking really good some will  see we're not gonna try to make  everything i don't have any mandate that  i must make a certain amount of game of  thrones successor shows or anything like  that we're really doing it just based on  what we're excited about creatively so  as you can see he doesn't really give us  any updates right here but he does say  something very interesting in his  following interview let me show you what  he said when he sat down at variety  during this interview casey said he  wasn't ready to announce when the series  might release or even hint at what time  of the year it might finally arrive just  yet  but yes the network is already thinking  about a renewal if you're better on  whether we're gonna do a second season i  think it's a good bet he said  but obviously we'll make preparations  ahead of time to make sure we're ahead  of the game he remains quiet on the  status of the other game of thrones  shows and development repeating his line  that right now there's one game of  thrones show that is green lit and that  is house of the dragon which we're  excited by i feel really good about what  i've seen so far as for any more green  light announcements i would never  announce it around the launch of a new  show whether to greenlight something or  not those are separate events alright  now since he didn't give very many  updates during his interview i want to  focus on what he said at the very end  because i think it's a very exciting  revelation as you can see he said he's  very excited about house of the dragon  and he feels really good about what he  has seen so far in fact he feels so good  about it he's already expecting the show  will be given a second season which is  very interesting if you ask me the way  hbo has been handling house of the  dragon is very different from how  they've handled many other shows  first of all they gave house of the  dragon a full series order without even  seeing a pilot episode which almost  never happens usually what a network  will do is order a pilot episode so they  can see if it's even good enough to  order a full season they did this with  game of thrones and basically every  other show they've ever made however for  some reason they did not do this with  house of the dragon  so without even seeing a single episode  not only did they order a full season  but now they're even expecting this new  series to be given a second season at 